{"agent_id":"pp3g-P9z2-read-only-db-audit-for-issue-313-crosslink-session-23","agent_seq":5,"timestamp":"2026-08-09T14:48:07.852133518Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"1566dff5-d465-4b23-a4bb-3f12073a22df","comment_uuid":"eb90ce99-2f81-4e88-ae0d-e78deb4a9a59","author":"pp3g-P9z2-read-only-db-audit-for-issue-313-crosslink-session-23","content":"## FINAL — Read-only DB audit: findings + cleanup plan (session 23)\n\nREAD-ONLY performed. No DB writes, no config changes, no binary/wrapper touch. All sqlite via `file:...?mode=ro` (a `PRAGMA wal_checkpoint` probe failed with read-only disk-I/O error, confirming enforcement).\n\n### 1. INVENTORY\n\n**FORK DB `~/.local/share/opencode/opencode-fork-pp3g.db`** — 1,142,870,016 B (1.064 GiB) + WAL 104,598,592 B (99.75 MiB), page_size 4096, page_count 279,343, freelist 0, integrity ok, WAL mode. **LIVE** (mtime updates as this session writes).\n- Tables: session **263** | message 1,534 | part 5,421 | event 19,472 | event_sequence 262 | project 3 | project_directory 73 | todo 14 | migration 38.\n- Session buckets: **'Say hi.' 168** | matrix-test 46 | real 27 | New-session 16 | matrix-other 4 | gate-test 3.\n- hang-model sessions: **235** (168 'Say hi.' + 67 matrix/gate/9x tests), agent=**build**, providerID=**hangtest** (title stored with literal JSON quotes: `\"Say hi.\"`).\n- 'Say hi.' created **2026-08-06 07:26 → 2026-08-08 04:48** (fork-verification era, dirs: /tmp/opencode/matrix-run*, /tmp/opencode/tl2b, ASES worktrees pp3g-TL2B/5WqO/6lNV/GlOB...).\n- Size by table (dbstat): **event 1,025 MiB (90%)** | message 49 MiB | part 11 MiB | indexes ~5 MiB.\n- **Dominant blob: ONE session** `ses_01bcae1e3ffe...` 'Pin retries=0 on title-gen path' (#273 hardening, deepseek-v4-flash/builder, 2026-08-09 01:48) = 970 MiB events (message.updated.1 with embedded diffs, single events up to 48 MB) + 48 MiB messages + 1.5 MiB parts ≈ **1,020 MiB ≈ 89% of the DB**.\n- 'Say hi.' flood total footprint: 1,765 events / 910 KB + 334 msgs / 109 KB + 285 parts / 18 KB ≈ **~1.03 MiB** — UI noise, negligible size.\n\n**MAIN DB `~/.local/share/opencode/opencode.db`** — 2,598,903,808 B (2.42 GiB) + WAL 9,286,512 B (8.86 MiB), page_count 634,915, freelist 0, WAL mode. Not live (mtime Aug 9 03:50).\n- Tables: session **698** | message 33,920 | part 141,533 | event 562,842 | event_sequence 1,039 | project 9 | project_directory 88 | todo 483 | session_message 42 | migration 38.\n- Session buckets: real **655** | New-session 43. **NO 'Say hi.' flood** (only 1 title containing 'Say'). 14 hang-model sessions exist (Aug 3-5, /tmp/opencode-hang-test, /tmp/opencode-145-patch, /tmp/opencode-11813-verify; 145 events/71 KB — tiny).\n- Sessions: 2026-06-21 17:55 → 2026-08-09 03:02.\n- Size by table: **event 1,977 MiB (76%)** | part 274 MiB | message 124 MiB. Top-10 sessions ≈ 965 MiB of events.\n- session.* events 41,683 (791 created + 40,892 updated); **793 distinct aggregates vs 698 session rows → ~95 sessions were already deleted, events retained** (evidence of prior pruning).\n- 'projects/ASES' occurrence counts: part 31,352 | message 28,361 | event 117,022 | session-directory 161.\n\n**BACKUP** `backups/opencode.db.pre-prune-20260808-175132/opencode.db` (1.9 GiB): 823 sessions, 38,825 msgs, 163,961 parts, 530,668 events → MAIN has since been pruned (823→698 sessions; msgs -4,905; parts -22,428) while events grew (+32,174). This backup is the pre-prune snapshot of the MAIN DB.\n\n**LOCAL DB `opencode-local.db`** (1 MiB + 478 KB WAL): 77 sessions, incl. **33 'Say hi.'** (hang-model/build, 2026-08-06 05:11-07:00).\n\n**Evidence reconciliation**: the pre-crash figures (~1,731 'Say hi.' / ~1,801 records; MAIN 41,488 sessions) are **not reproducible from current state** — they conflate event-row counts with session-row counts (e.g., 1,788 'hangtest' events ≈ 1,731; 41,683 session.* events ≈ 41,488). Current authoritative counts are above.\n\n### 2. WAL ASSESSMENT\n- FORK WAL 104 MB (~9% of file) holds un-checkpointed frames from live writes. `PRAGMA wal_checkpoint(TRUNCATE)` is safe/desirable **only when no opencode process has the DB open** (not now — live session). It fails under mode=ro by design.\n- MAIN WAL 9.3 MB — modest; checkpoint safe whenever the stock binary is not running.\n- opencode embeds `OPENCODE_DISABLE_AUTOCOMPACT` / `OPENCODE_DISABLE_PRUNE` knobs — the app has built-in compact/prune paths; prefer the app's session delete over raw SQL where possible.\n\n### 3. SESSION-STORE SPLIT MECHANISM (found)\n- **Baked-in channel string**: the fork binary embeds `var n=\"1.18.13-pp3g-fork\",t=\"fork-pp3g\"...`; the DB-layer names the DB from the channel: if `OPENCODE_DB` env set → use it; if channel ∈ {latest,beta,prod} or `OPENCODE_DISABLE_CHANNEL_DB=1` → `opencode.db`; **else → `opencode-<channel>.db`**.\n- Channel `fork-pp3g` → `opencode-fork-pp3g.db` in the data dir (`~/.local/share/opencode`). Stock binary → `opencode.db`.\n- No env override present (checked /proc/<pid>/environ: no OPENCODE_DB, no OPENCODE_CHANNEL). No DB key in `~/.config/opencode/opencode.json`; no `opencode.json` under `~/.local/share/opencode`. So the split is **entirely determined by which binary (fork vs stock) runs** — no config involved.\n\n### 4. SAFE CLEANUP PLAN (do NOT execute here — read-only mandate)\n**A. FORK 'Say hi.' + matrix/gate test junk (235 sessions)** — safe to prune; UI win (frees /sessions list), negligible size win (~1 MB).\n   1. Quiesce: exit ALL opencode processes (no live reader on the fork DB).\n   2. Backup: `sqlite3 opencode-fork-pp3g.db '.backup opencode-fork-pp3g.db.cleanup-backup'` (or stop-and-copy after a clean exit).\n   3. Prefer the fork's own path: REST `DELETE /session/{sessionID}` (binary shows 'Successfully deleted session'; TUI delete action) — app handles cascades.\n   4. Or documented SQL (FK: session→message→part cascade; event/event_sequence need explicit ordering):\n      `DELETE FROM event WHERE aggregate_id IN (SELECT id FROM session WHERE model LIKE '%hang-model%');`\n      `DELETE FROM event_sequence WHERE aggregate_id IN (...);`\n      `DELETE FROM session WHERE model LIKE '%hang-model%';`\n   5. While still idle: `PRAGMA wal_checkpoint(TRUNCATE);` then `VACUUM;` (or rely on app auto-compact).\n**B. Giant session `ses_01bcae1e3ffe...` (~1,020 MiB = 89% of fork DB)** — the actual size problem, likely the crash culprit. NOT junk (real builder session) → operator decision required. If disposable: same quiesce→backup→delete path (delete its events/event_sequence/message/part/session rows), reclaims ~1 GB.\n**C. MAIN DB** — already pruned; no urgent action. Optionally purge the ~95 orphaned aggregates' events (low value). Keep the pre-prune backup as archive.\n**D. WAL** — checkpoint only after quiesce; never against the live fork DB.\n**E. 'Say hi.' can be ignored for SIZE** (1 MB) but **should be pruned for UI hygiene**; not urgent.\n\n### 5. RECOMMENDATION ON THE SPLIT\n**Keep the separate fork DB.** Do not point the fork at opencode.db: the channel-named DB is by design (fork identity + upgrade-survival guard #274 depend on it), and merging stores would contaminate the real history with test sessions and destroy the isolation that made this diagnosis possible. The 'sessions gone' report is explained — the fork correctly reads its own DB; no data loss occurred. If a unified historical view is ever wanted, do it as a read-only external query/report, NOT by repointing the fork (repointing = config change + contamination risk, out of scope here).\n\nWHAT-NOT-TESTED: no DELETE/VACUUM/checkpoint executed (read-only mandate); the fork's REST session.delete path was not exercised end-to-end; FK cascade on session delete inferred from schema + observed orphaned events, not tested; WAL contents not frame-inspected (sizes only); repointing fork at opencode.db not attempted; evidence figures (~1,731/41,488) not reproducible from current state (see §1).","created_at":"2026-08-09T14:48:07.844571226Z","kind":"result","signed_by":"SHA256:QIpL7s0ZZ3NomkRchyZGKj1MYLta8icUBS0ESERcS28","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgAoXY/xDz2lySkQeeF/Wd4skDBzgq6CQxalZ7k0cSzxIAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAhp8jhT2DluAY5hZsm3cEn7WZsUX9aPKq5Enxynrl6T6y1fCwKVJ5HtkCtM7CrSgnxVuONs0Vi1bIIc/T4TFPAA=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:QIpL7s0ZZ3NomkRchyZGKj1MYLta8icUBS0ESERcS28","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgAoXY/xDz2lySkQeeF/Wd4skDBzgq6CQxalZ7k0cSzxIAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQLnzZGdpC3H0DItX0ZHwvQ+x4bRDCCgPPEXUUXuxD89bmmym32cd+FTssvIH/+JAwS7I/QrBbLQWsiOuGb0A6gg="}
